{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 5.0,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-25: rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is 3 and this trip counts if its fee stands, so the rider's account is flagged for review — mandatory upfront payment and temporary suspension pending Trust & Safety review; this referral does not change the ruling on the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your 5.00 SGD no-show fee stands. The record shows the driver reached the pickup at 08:29:10 — the nearest GPS fix (08:30:05) is 6.55 m from the pickup with 3 m reported accuracy, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and the 25 m accuracy filter (EV-GPS-05059, weight 1.0, arrival corroborated) — and your trip was on-demand, so under POL-NS-21 the 300-second free wait ran from arrival and expired at 08:34:10. The driver cancelled at 08:35:30, about 6 minutes 20 seconds after arriving and 80 seconds after the wait expired; that is not 'cancelled too fast'. Before cancelling he sent two in-app messages (08:29:30 and 08:32:45) and placed one in-app call (08:33:40, unanswered, 25 s), so POL-NS-23's contact obligation — at least one message AND at least one call, both before cancellation — is met. POL-NS-23 requires the driver to send and to call; it does not require you to read or answer. The chat log EV-CHAT-05059 is impaired at weight 0.85 on issue code UNREAD_MESSAGE precisely because neither message was opened; that corroborates that you did not see them, but the sent timestamps it records are unaffected, so the fee is not voided. POL-NS-24 does not assist you: this was an on-demand trip with no scheduled time (driver_deadline is null for exactly that reason), and the driver did arrive and wait out the free wait. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05059-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact under POL-GEN-02(3) and concerns route deviation, not a no-show fee. To the driver: under POL-NS-22 the 5.00 SGD fee stands and is transferred to you as compensation for time and fuel; the fare breakdown EV-FARE-05059 (weight 1.0) shows exactly 5.00 SGD charged and matching the policy fee, so both amount fields are 5.00 SGD. Confidence is 0.85: the message limb of the contact obligation is carried only by the impaired chat log EV-CHAT-05059 (0.85, UNREAD_MESSAGE) — the trip record attributes message_count and obligation_met to that same artifact, so it is not an independent carrier — and POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at that weight, while the arrival and the fee amount rest on complete 1.0 artifacts (trip record, GPS trace, fare breakdown). No escalation applies: the contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and neither party carries a fraud flag, so POL-NS-26 makes this AI ruling final. The POL-NS-25 referral above fires because the rider's 30-day no-show count reaches 3 counting this trip, and it never changes the ruling on the trip.",
    "_comment": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The 5.00 SGD should be held, not collected, on this record. The timeline POL-NS-24 works from cannot be fixed: this is an on-demand trip, and the trip record's own driver_deadline block returns deadline null with the reason 'on-demand trip: no scheduled time' — the very situation the note to POL-NS-24 sends to POL-GEN-26. The contact fact that the fee depends on is carried by impaired evidence, and the trace is one-sided: EV-GPS-05059 is a driver-device trace with rider_track [] and no rider-side artifact exists at all, so nothing in the record can check the rider's account. POL-GEN-26 makes escalation the disposition where a fact a rule needs cannot be established because the evidence carrying it is missing or impaired, and an escalated amount is held rather than charged to the rider.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-CHAT-05059 at weight_multiplier 0.85 but does not name its issue code(s): UNREAD_MESSAGE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "There is no open question calling for escalation under POL-GEN-26. Every fact this ruling needs — arrival, the running of the free wait, and pre-cancellation contact — is carried by COMPLETE artifacts. The only absent artifact is the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05059-01, which is MISSING at weight 0.0 and carries no fact under POL-GEN-02(3); a traffic advisory bears on route deviation, not on whether a no-show fee is due, so its absence leaves nothing undecided.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-05059-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Any attempt to decide this trip from the parties' histories is impermissible. driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags, prior_disputes_filed and prior_disputes_upheld, and rider_profile.rating, cancellation_rate and lifetime_trips, are CONTEXT ONLY under POL-GEN-01; they cannot establish a fact about TRP-05059 or ground its outcome, and only the two fraud-flag fields and the 30-day no-show count may be cited at all.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "PROFILE_FIELD_AS_GROUND",
      "detail": "relies_on names context-only profile field(s): prior_no_show_flags; POL-GEN-01 permits profile context but not a ground of decision"
    }
  ]
}
